WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.000
Long before there was a DC film universe,
Warner Bros. executives dreamed of a Justice

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:05.720
League movie.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.680
In fact, plans to bring the original super
friends together for a live-action outing

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.490
in theaters have been in various stages of
development for more than a decade—and the

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.000
project has taken far more than its share
of twists and turns along the way.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.380
From a derailed production to problematic
facial hair, here's the untold story of Justice

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:21.880
League.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.600
Summon the League

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.580
George Miller, who's best known as the mastermind
behind the Mad Max franchise, actually planned

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.970
to film a Justice League movie back in 2007—
when it would've beaten Marvel's Avengers

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.680
to theaters by several years and potentially
leveled the MCU-dominated Hollywood playing

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.180
field.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.820
Unfortunately, the project, called Justice
League: Mortal, was beset by a slew of problems,

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.240
including a writer's strike and an ongoing
battle over where to film the movie.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.200
In the end, the studio pulled the plug on
the film and went back to the drawing board,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.800
opting to launch their DC cinematic universe
with 2013's Man of Steel instead.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.520
Almost Affleck

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.860
For a brief window of time, Ben Affleck was
a frontrunner to direct the Justice League

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.860
movie, and we can only imagine how drastically
different the movie might've been if he had.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.340
Affleck's award-winning films like Gone Baby
Gone, The Town, and Argo prove that he's got

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.620
the ability to write, direct, and star in
movies that get raves from critics and audiences

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.120
alike.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.220
And given the bumpy road the DC extended universe
has faced with critics thus far, it isn't

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.149
hard to understand why the idea of a Justice
League movie with some of Affleck's trademark

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:24.020
seriousness and grit might be appealing.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.100
But the rumors turned out not to be true—

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.100
"Don't believe everything you hear, son."

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.400
— and that was only the start of the movie's
directorial difficulties.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.180
Enter: Joss Whedon

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.740
After Man of Steel and Dawn of Justice, Zack
Snyder was supposed to direct Justice League,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:38.240
as well.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.820
But when a personal tragedy forced him to
step away from the project, one friend was

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.200
ready to step in and save the day: Avengers
director Joss Whedon.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.120
With a little convincing from his buddy Zack,
Whedon took the reins and saddled up to handle

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.759
his third massive superhero ensemble flick
within the past five years.

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:56.499
And he didn't take the job lightly: Whedon
went to town, making so many changes that

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.580
he earned himself a writer's credit for contributing
more than thirty-three percent of the screenplay.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.260
Over budget

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.340
With great rewrites come great responsibility—and
a bigger budget.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.560
Between the studio's notes and Whedon's retooled
script, Justice League's supersized budget

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.920
required an extra $25 million for reshoots,
not to mention an extra two months on the

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.400
set for all the actors involved.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.140
It just goes to show that Warner Bros. wanted
the movie to be the best it could — or at

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.360
least better than the last one.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.640
The million-dollar mustache

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.100
Of all the time and money spent on reshoots,
a significant percentage went into digitally

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.000
erasing Henry Cavill's mustache.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.880
Cavill was already at work on a new film by
the time the studio needed their Superman

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.221
back, and although producers managed to finagle
a blockbuster timesharing deal, the actor

00:02:38.221 --> 00:02:42.370
had to keep this magnificent cookie duster
intact for his role on the next Mission Impossible

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.300
flick — which left it up to DC's digital
wizards to remove it in post-production.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.480
Funny on purpose

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.980
If you didn't love the dark tone of DC's previous
movies, take heart—Justice League is reportedly

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.900
amping up the comedy after Batman v Superman
took a critical pounding for being too serious.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.100
As Zack Snyder put it:

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.530
"Because of what fans have said and how the
movie was received by some … we have put

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.540
the screws to what we thought the tone would
be."

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.790
Evidence of the change was already visible
in the Justice League trailers, which suggest

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:13.120
that this is one superhero movie that's not
afraid to poke fun at itself.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.320
"What are your superpowers again?"

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.880
"I'm rich."

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.480
April Fools

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.680
After the release of Dawn of Justice, Warner
Bros. started gearing up for pre-production

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.831
on Justice League in April 2016—only to
have director Zack Snyder abruptly exit the

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.000
film entirely after throwing an epic, public
temper tantrum.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:31.680
The twist?

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.700
It was all an April Fool's Day gag — albeit
one that's less funny in hindsight, since

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.860
Snyder actually did depart the film a year
later after the tragic loss of his daughter.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.760
There can be only one

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.880
When Warner Bros. initially unveiled its massive
slate of DC movies, there were two Justice

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.840
League projects on the docket—one slated
for 2017, with a sequel to come two years

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:51.340
later.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.460
But after a tumultuous year for the DC Extended
Universe, the studio changed its approach

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.140
to take things one film at a time.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.900
Will we still end up getting a Justice League
sequel?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.600
Probably, but it'll happen the old-fashioned
way—with an announcement issued after the

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.640
studio counts its cash.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.700
The end of Batfleck?

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:11.220
Although he's denied it repeatedly, rumors
continue to swirl that Ben Affleck is planning

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.220
to hang up his Batsuit.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.580
It's not hard to see why he might want out
of the DC universe—his first outing at Batman

00:04:16.591 --> 00:04:20.539
took a critical drubbing, Justice League had
a lot of hiccups on its way to theaters, and

00:04:20.539 --> 00:04:24.909
the solo Batman movie that he was originally
supposed to write, star in, and direct still

00:04:24.909 --> 00:04:26.490
doesn't have a release date on the books.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.139
Will Affleck pull off a Batman-style disappearing
act in real life, creeping into the shadows

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.520
never to be seen again by the execs at WB?

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:39.160
"Oh wow, they really just vanished, Oh…
that's rude."

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.000
For now, he claims he's happy to play the
caped crusader.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.300
We'll see how long that lasts.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.380
Thanks for watching!

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.680
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.180
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

